  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening program interventions towards malaria elimination in DPR Korea - Korea (Democratic Peoples Republic) (01-Mar-2015-31-Mar-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Korea (Democratic Peoples Republic), Malaria, United Nations Children&apos;s Fund (UNICEF)This program has the following goals: To reduce malaria incidence in all high risk Ris to less than 3.0/1000 by the year 2017.  To reduce overall malaria incidence by 70% of the 2011 level by 2017. The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: To identify and delimit the foci of malaria transmission and eliminate it through well-targeted interventions (Strategic objective 7.1).  Objective 2: To provide quality-assured diagnosis and effective treatment (Strategic objective 7.2).  Objective 3: To strengthen the managerial and technical capacities for malaria pre-elimination (Strategic objective 7.3).  Objective 4: To strengthen partnership, multi-sector participation and international collaboration for malaria elimination (Strategic objective 7.4).  Objective 5: To improve strategic information for malaria elimination (Strategic objective 7.5)</narrative>
  </description>
